@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix delphi: <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/> .

sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch03-07> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kernel-checked Lean 4 statement about a model: If weight is k times the cube of a linear dimension (isometric growth at constant density), the log-log exponent of weight on that dimension is exactly 3 and the weight ratio is the cube of the size ratio; a measured exponent other than 3 refutes the exact cube law on that interval." ;
    dct:description "If weight is k times the cube of a linear dimension (isometric growth at constant density), the log-log exponent of weight on that dimension is exactly 3 and the weight ratio is the cube of the size ratio; a measured exponent other than 3 refutes the exact cube law on that interval." ;
    dct:source "On Growth and Form (1917)" ;
    skos:notation "W \\propto L^3 whatever the law of growth L(t)" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **The log-log exponent of a cube law is exactly 3.** -/
theorem cubeLaw_loglog_exponent {W : ℝ → ℝ} {k : ℝ} (h : CubeLaw W k) {L₁ L₂ : ℝ} (h₁ : 0 < L₁)
    (h₂ : 0 < L₂) (hne : L₁ ≠ L₂) : logSlope W L₁ L₂ = 3"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.CubeLaw" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.cubeLaw_loglog_exponent", "Delphi.cubeLaw_ratio", "Delphi.not_cubeLaw_of_exponent_ne_three" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Exact form only: W = k L^3 (isometric growth at constant density) gives a log-log exponent of exactly 3 and weight ratio (L2/L1)^3; a measured exponent other than 3 refutes the exact law on that interval. Thompson's \"mainly (though not wholly)\" and the claim test's tolerance band are outside the theorem." ;
    skos:note "The claim as the source states it, which is NOT what the kernel checked: \"Weight tends to vary as the cube of linear dimensions during growth\" (On Growth and Form, 1917). What was checked is the statement in dct:description, which is about a model." ;

    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: A single linear dimension L and mass W of one body family; fixed shape and constant density are what W = k L^3 encodes; Thompson's \"mainly (though not wholly)\" is not formalised: the theorem is exact, the law is approximate, and the tolerance band [2.5, 3.5] the claim test uses is a decision rule outside the module; No data enters the module; the measured exponents are read from the claims thread's result files and pointed to. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Thompson.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-07> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch03-07> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-thompson1917-ch03-07> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-thompson1917-ch03-07> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.cubeLaw_loglog_exponent with zero sorry and standard axioms; it also rejected 2 deliberately broken variant(s) of this statement or its model" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.3 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Thompson.lean (70 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.cubeLaw_loglog_exponent, Delphi.cubeLaw_ratio, Delphi.not_cubeLaw_of_exponent_ne_three: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T22:57:06.367Z): 2 deliberate change(s) to this statement or its model were each rejected by the compiler: [elimination-certificate-false-claim] Certificate sabotaged: the giant-insect elimination is rewritten to claim that a weight ratio of exactly 10^6 at length ratio 100 is ruled out. It is not (10^6 = 100^3), so norm_num must fail and the kernel must reject the certificate. Rejected with 1 error(s): Eliminations.lean:16:100: error: unsolved goals [thompson-exponent-two] Statement changed to claim the log-log exponent of a cube law is 2 instead of 3. Rejected with 2 error(s): Thompson.lean:53:60: error: unsolved goals Controls: 17 of 17 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch03-07> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: A single linear dimension L and mass W of one body family; fixed shape and constant density are what W = k L^3 encodes; Thompson's \"mainly (though not wholly)\" is not formalised: the theorem is exact, the law is approximate, and the tolerance band [2.5, 3.5] the claim test uses is a decision rule outside the module; No data enters the module; the measured exponents are read from the claims thread's result files and pointed to. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

